  "facts": [
    "Opened on 5 September 1980, the Gotthard Road Tunnel was the world’s longest road tunnel at 16.9 kilometres, a record it held until 2002 and a milestone for Swiss motorway engineering.",
    "The tunnel’s single bore houses two lanes, one each direction, and features four ventilation shafts plus a side gallery with its own system—built to allow a future second tunnel if traffic demands rise.",
    "After a fatal 2001 collision and fire that killed eleven, the tunnel closed for two months; since then, no more than 150 trucks per hour may enter, dramatically tightening safety protocols."
